La Trobe Advancement Responsibilities
(15)
The La Trobe Advancement will be responsible for:
Approving all fundraising activities undertaken in the name of La Trobe University;
Advising the University Executive (including the Vice-Chancellor, Deputy Vice-Chancellors, Pro Vice-Chancellors, ) and other University staff on issues related to fundraising;
The ongoing operation of the La Trobe University Foundation;
Initiating and co-ordinating fundraising campaigns;
Bequest and planned giving programs;
Prospect research and tracking;
Donor stewardship;
Managing and maintaining all data on fundraising in the University.

Information required by La Trobe Advancement
(19)
In order to determine whether a fundraising project may be approved, the following information needs to be provided to the La Trobe Advancement.
The name of the local officer(s) responsible for the implementation and management of the fundraising activity/campaign;
The outcomes expected/desired from the fundraising activity/campaign;
Resources to be applied to the fundraising activity;
The specific purpose to which funds raised will be allocated;
The timeframe for the activity (including a wrap up date, if appropriate);
Any evidence of potential donors;
Statement of how the project fits with the University’s strategic priorities.
